# Ignore file for tools/check-secrets.sh
#
# One glob pattern per line, matched against the repo-relative path ONLY -
# never against the path as it was typed on the command line. Every path is
# resolved to an absolute path first and then made relative to the repo
# root, so "./vars/x.yml", "vars/x.yml" and an absolute path all normalise
# to the same thing and the pattern "vars/*.example.yml" covers all three.
# Write patterns repo-relative: an absolute-form pattern will not match.
# (A path outside the repo has no relative form, so its absolute path is
# used.) Blank lines and lines starting with '#' are skipped. Use
# `--no-ignore` to disable this file, and `--list-ignored` to see exactly
# what it is hiding and why.

# Placeholder documentation, never deployed - these are illustrative
# defaults (e.g. "password: password") that ship as templates for operators
# to copy and fill in, not real credentials.
vars/*.example.yml

# Deliberately-bad inputs for this script's own test suite. They must keep
# failing the scan for the tests to mean anything; run
# `check-secrets.sh --no-ignore tools/fixtures` to exercise them.
tools/fixtures/*

# The mysql-cluster HA-supervisor component's database password is an ordinary
# dictionary word that is also the name of a directory these two files
# reference. Every match in them is that directory name in a path, not a
# written-out credential. Exempt until the password is rotated; delete these
# two lines then and the matches disappear on their own.
tasks/mysql-cluster/start.yml
templates/mysql-cluster/docker-compose.yml.j2
